<title>BELGIUM: No official EU comment on Boeing planned Tuesday.</title>
<headline>No official EU comment on Boeing planned Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Tuesday it did not plan any official statement in the wake of Washington's clearance without conditions of Boeing Co's merger with McDonnell Douglas Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;We do not plan any statement tonight,&quot; a spokesman for EU Competition Commissioner Karel Van Miert told Reuters.</p>
<p>The U.S. Federal Trade Commission on Tuesday unconditionally approved the $14 billion merger of U.S. aircraft manufacturer Boeing Co. and former rival McDonnell Douglas, helping clear the way for creation of the world's largest aircraft maker.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
